 "inference": [
  "Against tanks, EA's range for a direct-hit weapon is registry direct damage times the grid value times 0.75 (rounded up) to times 2. This is exact for six weapons. The top factor 2 equals Field_7fa53094, stored as 2 in every cell read; that the field is the cap is an inference from the equal value.",
  "Against helicopters and jets there is no such factor: EA's figure is direct damage times its grid value plus blast damage times the blast material's grid value, exact for the same six weapons, with jets capped at 1000.",
  "Mines (L3321) are the blast-only case of the same rule. The registry default is the number that fits in every case, which supports L3318.",
  "The mobile anti-air figures of L3322 are twice what this rule gives for aircraft (26, 32.5, 100, 65 against 52, 65, 200, 130). They are the one group that does not fit; that factor stays untraced."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "The hit-quality factor between 0.75 and 2 is not tied to the stored angle curves of L3201. Test: fire tank HE at a tank's front, side and rear from 20 m and read the damage; 180 and 480 are the stored extremes.",
  "The mobile anti-air factor 2. Test: one high velocity rocket hit on a full-health helicopter; 26 means EA counts a pair, 52 means a further multiplier exists.",
  "Heavy Rockets, RPG and tank APFSDS fit only with earlier damage values. Test: one RPG hit on a tank's rear on the current build should read 500 (125 x 2 x 2); one tank APFSDS hit on a tank's rear should read 650.",
  "Only the Abbasid grid was read for these cells. Test: repeat one tank HE rear hit on a second map; 480 on both confirms the grid values are shared."
 ],
 "siteImpact": "None. No Analyzer data, simulation or UI change.",
